<title>BELGIUM: EU tells Spain to recover 1.9 bln ptas from CASA.</title>
<headline>EU tells Spain to recover 1.9 bln ptas from CASA.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had ordered Spain to recover 1.9 billion pesetas ($13.1 million) in aid granted to national aircraft maker Construcciones Aeronauticas (CASA).</p>
<p>It said in a statement that CASA had received more money than allowed under EU rules on subsidies to research and development projects and noted that the aided project was stopped halfway through its completion.</p>
<p>CASA received a 7.2-billion-peseta loan between 1991 and 1993 to finance the development of a turbo propeller aircraft with 70 to 80 seats. The Commission said the reimbursement of 1.9 billion pesetas would restore fair competition.</p>
<p>CASA is the smallest of the four Airbus Industrie partners.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841 ($ = 145.4 Spanish Pesetas)</p>
